<title>RUSSIA: Russian non-CIS H1 aluminium exports rise 31 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian non-CIS H1 aluminium exports rise 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's exports of aluminium outside the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) in the first six months of this year were 1.30 million tonnes, which was 31 percent more than in the same 1995 period, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exports of nickel over January-June to countries outside the CIS rose four percent to 70,300 tonnes, and exports of copper over the same period to the same destinations rose 32 percent to 244,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures-</p>
<p>		  RUSSIAN NON-FERROUS METALS EXPORTS TO NON-CIS</p>
<p>				     DESTINATIONS</p>
<p>				   June 1996  May 1996  June 1995</p>
<p>Aluminium</p>
<p> month/month pct change	  -1	  -4	   +2</p>
<p> year/year pct change	   +22	 +26	   -7</p>
<p>Nickel</p>
<p> month/month pct change	 -52	  -6	   +3</p>
<p> year/year pct change	   -47	 +15	  +51</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> month/month pct change	 -39	 -10	   +4</p>
<p> year/year pct change	   -20	 +36	   +1</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
